/-!
# Marked placement in Held's supplied normal A₆ section

The dihedral quotient forces pi*mu into the supplied section. The earlier
source fusions pi~pi*lambda and pi~pi*xi select the remaining two memberships;
the normalization hypotheses recover exactly the supplied marking from the
source's binary choices.

The imported modules prove these reductions. The existence of the earlier
source inputs and the symmetric-extension and lambda-centralization arguments
remain obligations before `MarkedSection` can be constructed.

Source: D. Held, Illinois J. Math. 13 (1969), 224–240,
DOI 10.1215/ijm/1256053756, Lemma 4.2, pp.232–235.
-/
